SEVER-DB Part 4: the erasure

Inserted 6 records (encrypted, d = 16); the person to forget owns ["note-1", "note-4"].

1. Positive control: the scanner RECOVERS note-1's vector on the image (67 records, 5 key slots carved).

2. delete_user ["note-1", "note-4"]:
   certificate 1741 bytes, database_lsn 6: operator signature and deletion proof verify (C_S pre → post).
   certificate 1709 bytes, database_lsn 7: operator signature and deletion proof verify (C_S pre → post).

3. Checkpoint, shut down, scan the image for the deleted records: 0 findings (control note-0 still recovered).

4. The leak, made visible: run `scripts/demo-p4.sh` (it builds the SB-24 variant) to see
   the same scan decrypt the deleted records when group-key rotation is skipped.

5. Crash during phase C (after COMMIT, acknowledged: false); on restart 3 records remain and
   recovery erased the old key. New scan: 0 findings.

